  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 480,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The entire petrodollar system is supposedly once \nagain under threat now that Iran floated asking  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7440,
    "dDurationMs": 8560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tankers passing through the Strait of Hormuz \nto pay in Chinese yuan rather than in dollars.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16000,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's just one tiny problem, though. If you \njust look at the numbers, the entire idea of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21920,
    "dDurationMs": 8480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the petro dollar system quickly reveals itself as \nthe biggest myth in geopolitics. That being said,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30400,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as with any good myth, there are, of course, some \nelements of truth to it. For example, it is true  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37200,
    "dDurationMs": 8560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that in the summer of 1974, the US under Nixon \nand Saudi Arabia under King Faisal, signed one  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45760,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the most economically and geopolitically \nrelevant agreements of the 20th century,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50880,
    "dDurationMs": 8720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which saw the establishment of a so-called \nUS-Saudi joint commission on economic cooperation.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59600,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, for a long time, the details of that \nagreement were a secret, which is probably how  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65440,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we ended up with the myth of the establishment of \nthe petrodollar system in the first place. And it  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71840,
    "dDurationMs": 9360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "roughly goes like this: In 1971, Nixon abandoned \nthe gold standard, creating significant US dollar  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81200,
    "dDurationMs": 10080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "volatility and inflation in the United States. \nThen in 1973, the US was hit by a big oil crisis,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91280,
    "dDurationMs": 7760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which was caused primarily by Saudi Arabia and on \nother Arab nations that cut supply in general and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99040,
    "dDurationMs": 7520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "embargoed oil to any nation who supported Israel \nin their war against Syria and Egypt. And as you  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106560,
    "dDurationMs": 7520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can see here, that caused a massive spike in \noil prices, fuel shortages in the US, and it  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114080,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "significantly raised inflation. Then we get to our \nfamous agreement. In 1974, the US and Saudi Arabia  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121040,
    "dDurationMs": 9680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "signed it, which stated that from the Saudi side, \nthey would only sell in US dollars. Number one.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130720,
    "dDurationMs": 7600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then point number two, they would invest those \ndollars into the United States itself, and this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138320,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would be called recycling petro dollars ,and these \nwere then recycled into US banks and treasuries.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145200,
    "dDurationMs": 7840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But of course, this would not be for free. On the \nother hand, the US would defend Saudi Arabia and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153040,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "help them to get started economically. 1974 was \nthe start of the petrodollar system. The US dollar  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159200,
    "dDurationMs": 7600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was now backed by oil and this cemented the US \ndollar's status as the unquestioned global reserve  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166800,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "currency. The importance of the petrodollar could \nthen also explain that every time a nation like  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172640,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Iran or Iraq or Venezuela announced that they \nwould start selling oil in another currency,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178560,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the US would put a stop to this because of course \nthis undermined the fundamental power of the US  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185120,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dollar. Very convincing sounding story. And while \nthe story about the founding of the petrodollar  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190880,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "system is at least a little bit closer to the \ntruth than the modern-day petrodollar story,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196240,
    "dDurationMs": 8240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the fundamentals underlying it are still a big fat \nmyth. And how do we know? Well, luckily for us,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204480,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bloomberg News requested the release of the \nexact details of the US-Saudi 1974 deal in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210880,
    "dDurationMs": 8160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "2016 under the US Freedom of Information Law. So, \nwhat does it say? Well, here are the previously  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219040,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "confidential documents detailing how the Nixon \nadministration believed that this deal would  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 226080,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "work and why it would help America. It says \"the \ncommission was established on the heels of the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232880,
    "dDurationMs": 8400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Arab oil embargo and price increases. The embargo \nemphasized that closer US Arab ties were needed.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241280,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The oil price increases gave Saudi Arabia \na substantial amount of petrodollars which  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246960,
    "dDurationMs": 7840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could be used for development purposes.\" So, two \nthings stand out to me. Focus on price increases,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254800,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then number two, we already have a mention \nof petrodollars here. So, petrodollars themselves  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 259440,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are not a myth. Continuing the commission was \nperceived as an important mechanism for number  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264880,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one, fostering closer political ties between \nthe two countries through economic cooperation,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270320,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "assisting Saudi industrialization and \ndevelopment, while there we have it,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 274640,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "recycling petrodollars. So recycling petrodollars \nis absolutely in there. And then number three,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281120,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "facilitating the flow to Saudi Arabia of American \ngoods, services, and technology. And then finally,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287280,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it says, \"In helping the Saudis to find a way to \ninvest their large and growing financial reserves,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292080,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we will give them added incentives to continue \nto produce oil in the quantity needed to meet  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 297200,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "world demand. And this is crucial: \"at a \nstable and hopefully lower price levels.\" So,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303600,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "takeaway number one, what really stood out \nto me, no mention at all whatsoever in these  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309760,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "documents of the Saudis committing to pricing oil \nin US dollars or the US finding this important.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315840,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was not important. And this is actually backed \nup by other evidence presented by the Yaw Asamoah  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322400,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Substack which found that the Saudis actually kept \naccepting British pounds for oil for quite a while  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 328160,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "after the 1974 agreement, which we now have seen \nis not surprising given that it was not part of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 334560,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that agreement. So in summary, what is myth and \nwhat is reality when it comes to the establishment  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340720,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the petrodollar system? Well, first, let's \nlook at what the US gives according to the myth:  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347280,
    "dDurationMs": 7440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "economic development and security. And according \nto reality, yeah, that's also the case. But then  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 354720,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "here are the major differences Saudi gives. Well, \nrecycling petrodollars and reducing borrowing  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 361440,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "costs potentially for the US. Yeah, that was \ndefinitely in there. But what was absolutely  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 367520,
    "dDurationMs": 8960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not in there is US dollar transaction exclusivity \nnot the case. The thing that was in there clearly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 376480,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a couple of times was oil price stability. And \nthis is crucial because it changes the story about  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383760,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the US motivation for this agreement completely. \nThe myth is: it was about supporting the dominance  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 390400,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the dollar. Not true at all. What matters is \noil price stability. And this will honestly make  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397360,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a lot of sense once we start looking at the other \nsupporting data. The US did not need to make some  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 402640,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fancy deal for people to price their oil exports \nexclusively in US dollars. The South American  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 409040,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "copper men were already invoicing their exports in \ndollars. The European industrialists, the Japanese  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414480,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "industrialists, all of them invoiced their \nexports in dollars mostly already. And everyone  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 420480,
    "dDurationMs": 8720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "did it because by 1974, the dollar was already the \nundisputed global reserve currency. It's actually  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429200,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more likely that this dominance had been cemented \nby something called eurodollars rather than by  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436160,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "petrodollars. But if you want to learn more about \nthat, I have to refer you to potentially the best  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 442560,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "economics course that I've ever taken. And that \nis now available via our advertising sponsor,  "
    } ]
  }, {
